  "conclusions": [
    "VOLT1/2 did not enter capture. MODE/ROWS ACK+terminal+CONFIG succeeded; no MFAULT/RST/FATAL was recorded. One or more read-only query replies were not observed before their bounded deadline.",
    "Device RX bytes and priority queue admissions account for all issued commands and applied events; firmware accepted-byte deltas plus final query bytes exactly equal recorded raw bytes. This supports loss after priority queue admission and before driver acceptance, rather than a collector read/parser omission. Per-class/per-packet TX loss counters are absent, so attribution to each missing reply is aggregate evidence plus the production code path.",
    "VOLT3 recorded 120.00009842999862 seconds with 3766 CRC-valid parsed frames. Two actual K lines ended after comma-ses, omitting session/bootId/rev. Headers matched CONFIG. The strict identity failure is valid; the more precise category is transport/trailer truncation, not configuration domain inconsistency.",
    "SerialIo uses one 20ms whole-packet deadline for both priority and normal queues, 64-byte nonblocking writes, and vTaskDelay(1) on backpressure. At 100Hz this retry delay is 10ms. An expired packet is discarded; a partially emitted packet is delimited by LF before the next packet. This explains the observed wire shape. Which scheduler/bus contention caused an individual timeout is not proven by these logs."
  ],
